# Cursor & Kiro Agent Rules for CyBridge

- Always inspect `AGENTS.md` and `.kiro/instructions.md` before making architectural modifications. `AGENTS.md` is the source of truth; `ARCHITECTURE.md` describes how the system works.
- There is one backend: Python/FastAPI in `backend/app/`. Backend changes go there, respecting its layers (routers → services → repositories). The React app is in `frontend/`; Node only builds it.
- Keep all Gemini API calls server-side — `backend/app/ai.py` (`google-genai`, model `gemini-3.6-flash`). Never expose `GEMINI_API_KEY` to the browser.
- Schema changes are new migrations in `backend/app/migrations.py`; never edit `backend/app/schema_sql.py`.
- Verify frontend changes from `frontend/` with `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`) and `npm run build`.
- Verify backend changes with `backend/.venv/Scripts/python -m pytest backend/tests` and `python backend/scripts/verify_authz_scenarios.py http://localhost:8000` — it must stay 65/65.
- Build pages from the shared primitives in `frontend/src/components/ui/` and the theme tokens in `frontend/src/index.css`, so all six themes apply.
- Keep camera and microphone access in the interview agent graceful: ask, explain, and fall back when permission is denied.
